anatomy, normal values, methodology;
Hemodynamics and gradients:
what is important to measure and why;
Aortic valve:
stenosis, regurgitation, SVD, thrombosis, endocarditis;
Mitral valve:
stenosis, regurgitation, SVD, PPM, PVL;
Prosthetic valve dysfunction:
structural and non-structural, ESC/EACTS 2025 criteria, thrombosis, PPM, endocarditis, PVL;
Quantitative assessment:
EOA, DVI, PISA, EROA, vena contracta, PHT, etc.;
Complex cases and differential diagnosis:
mixed lesions, low flow/low gradient, etc.;
Hemodynamic consequences and associated conditions:
PH, chamber remodeling, LA, LV;
Practical reviews and clinical cases:
interactive session, analysis of echocardiography protocols;

